Z||000008||pherder||07-16-2000||06:52 PM||||Call Kirk for current prices but as of 2 years ago they were:<P>$395 for the roll bar<BR>$595 for the roll cage<BR>+ shipping<P>The bar I have does NOT get in the way of anything!  It mounts in 4 places, 2 bottom mounts and two rear firewall mounts.  Now that I think of it, I did have to move the relays (fuel and A/C) because that is where the upper mount on the left side ended up at.  <P>As you can see by the picture of Curt Martin's cage, the current style bar/cage has the straight across bar right thru where the ECM is.<P>I had to special order my bar to get the "old" style.  And since I wasn't really going racing with the car (I was going to make the car into a convertible and wanted the added roll over protection that I would have removed), I didn't care if it met SCCA's rules.  Now that the convertible project has died due to lack of support by the "manufacturer", the roll bar is in there for "OHHH!" factor.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||PJ||07-16-2000||08:37 PM||||The Kirk design started out as a SCCA legal Showroom Stock design. It was made to clear the 3rd stoplight & the console over the ECM, since removing interior pieces is a no-no in SS. A L-shaped bend of pipe was added to the driver's side main hoop (roll-bar) so you could attach the shoulder belts. You can see it in pherders photo behind the driver's seat. The SCCA decided to change (add to) the reinforcement of the main hoop a couple of years ago. They mandated a horizontal bar across the total width of the main hoop so Kirk ditched the L-shaped pipe and just ran one straight across at belt mounting level. Fiero's were no longer classed in Showroom stock so he didn't worry about clearing trim and interior pieces.<P>lowCG: Since my main hoop is the old style I ran a horizontal bar at belt height from the passenger side down tube to the diagonal, then a higher one (to clear the ECM) from the diagonal to the L-shaped pipe on the drivers side.<P>It is interesting that pherder's picture of Kurt Martin's cage would not be SCCA legal today. They recently added a requirement for a petty bar (diagonal from the foot of the front passenger side down tube to the top of the main hoop by the driver) or braces running back from the main hoop, through the rear window, to the rear strut towers. I run with the rear braces and it stiffens the chassis up quite a bit. I think I paid about $480 in '93 for the cage with two extra side bars.<P>Bottom Line: If you want to keep your interior intact you need to order the old style!<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||07-17-2000||12:44 PM||||Paeco Imports also makes a BAR or cage for the fiero. Just ordered a cage for a nother car. And asked while talking to them about a fiero cage is't not $500+ any more.. their $320 SCCA approved. Have 6-8 week turn around time and your credit card will not be charged untill it goes into production (which is about 1 week before it's shipped) ||||reg||1
